for supabase migrations, use `supabase migrations new` rather than manually creating the file
my created_by fields reference public.users and not auth.users
NEVER change data in my remote database or apply migrations through the supabase MCP / psql / supabase db push. All changes should ONLY be done through my automated CICD unless I EXPLICITLY tell you otherise. Test migrations and changes locally first.

The bible structure tables (bible_versions, books, chapters, verses) use text ids rather than uuids. The rest of my tables use uuid ids
 
Code Style and Structure
- Write clean, maintainable, and technically accurate TypeScript code. - Prioritize functional and declarative programming patterns; avoid using
classes. - Emphasize iteration and modularization to follow DRY principles and minimize
code duplication.

RBAC and RLS
- Use has_permission(user_id, action_key, resource_type, resource_id) in RLS policies for shared tables (e.g., projects) instead of ad-hoc checks.
- Tables with user_id should continue to use simple user_id = auth.uid() policies.
- Roles are scoped per context via user_roles(user_id, role_id, context_type, context_id).
- Permissions are defined in role_permissions(role_id, resource_type, permission_key, is_allowed). Do not hardcode permission strings in policies.
- Inheritance paths for project access: direct role → team membership via projects_teams → base via bases_teams → partner via partner_orgs_projects.